---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Palworld 1.0 Guide Hub and Our Editorial Standards"
  description="Learn how the unofficial Palworld 1.0 Guide Hub separates Pocketpair-confirmed facts from player-tested recommendations, maintains sources, and avoids unverified rankings."
  canonical="/about/"
>
  <section class="page-hero compact">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>About Palworld 1.0 Guide Hub</h1>
    <p>An unofficial English guide site built to turn Palworld 1.0's official changes into practical player checklists without presenting speculation as fact.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="text-page">
    <figure class="article-visual">
      <img src="/assets/palworld-guide-hero.png" alt="Fan-made Palworld 1.0 Guide Hub fantasy island artwork" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>Fan-made artwork created for this independent guide project; no official key art or screenshot is used.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      Palworld 1.0 Guide Hub is an unofficial fan-made site for practical questions: how to start, what returning players should inspect, how to protect a save, how to update a server, and which Version 1.0 facts are officially confirmed.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <p>
      This is not a complete Wiki, scraped database, official news source, or replacement for Pocketpair's announcements. It does not publish Best Pals, Best Weapons, Best Base Locations, exact routes, or precise server multipliers without adequate player testing.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
    <p>
      Palworld 1.0 is live and the official v1.0 changelog is available. Official facts are paraphrased and linked to primary sources. Hardware results, routes, rankings, MOD compatibility, server capacity and balance-sensitive recommendations are labeled when they still need in-game verification.
    </p>

    <h2>How to use the guides</h2>
    <p>Start with the Short answer, use the tables and checklists for immediate action, then read Source notes and verification warnings before making irreversible changes to a save, server, base or rare-resource investment.</p>

    <h2>Artwork and independence</h2>
    <p>Site visuals are original fan-made illustrations or information graphics. The site does not use Pocketpair's Logo, official key art, unauthorized screenshots, or other guide sites' images. Palworld and related names belong to their respective owners.</p>

    <div class="compact-link-grid">
      <a href="/guides/"><strong>Browse player guides</strong></a>
      <a href="/server/"><strong>Browse server guides</strong></a>
      <a href="/palworld-1-0/palworld-1-0-patch-notes-explained/"><strong>Read Patch Notes Explained</strong></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
